## Goal
Make the app's quit path in the handler (DEV-47) deliver links that are still queued or in flight, instead of terminating immediately and dropping them.

## Problems
The session slice shows no work on this commit's file. It only holds a subagent report about a related race fix in `internal/handler/panel.m`: a link arriving during shutdown could show a panel after termination had started. That is a separate commit. Beyond that, the logic is Objective-C run-loop timing, so no pure Go logic could be unit-tested and no manual quit test was run in the slice.

## Decision
In `internal/handler/handler.m`, `applicationShouldTerminate` no longer returns `NSTerminateNow`. It always returns `NSTerminateLater` and replies to the quit after a 150 ms grace once the inflight count is 0. If links are still in flight, it replies when the last one finishes, after the grace. The idle quit goes through `NSApp terminate:`, so it takes the same path. This gives queued links time to be delivered, and one code path handles every quit.

## Rejected
None. A Go unit test was skipped because the behavior depends only on Objective-C run-loop timing.

